course: dictionary
lesson: 13550
title: Impromptu: made on the spur of the moment
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Impromptu means done without planning or practice. Someone decides in a moment and does it straight away. You say it im-PROMPT-too. It can be an adjective, as in «an impromptu speech», or an adverb, as in she spoke impromptu.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Mum did not know we were coming, so she made an impromptu lunch of toast and soup.» The words did not know tell you nobody planned the lunch. Made tells you it was done quickly, so impromptu means unplanned.
explain: Try the swap check. Put "made up on the spur of the moment" into the sentence in place of impromptu. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning. «An impromptu party» is a party that starts with no plan, like when friends arrive and someone puts the music on.
fact: Impromptu means done or made without planning or practice.
fact: «An impromptu speech» is a talk you give with no time to prepare.
fact: Drama classes use impromptu acting, which is also called improvisation.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad bursts into impromptu songs about himself.
fact: In music, an impromptu is a short piece that sounds as if it were made up on the spot.
exercise: «We had an impromptu party when the rain stopped.» What does impromptu mean here? | Held indoors | *Made up on the spur of the moment | Very loud and long | Planned weeks before
exercise: Mr Hale asked Sam for an impromptu talk. What is an impromptu talk? | A talk that lasts all day | A talk given in the library | A talk read from a written script | *A talk given with no preparation
exercise: «The band played an impromptu tune at the end of the show.» Which word means made up without planning? | *impromptu | show | tune | band
test: Toad sings impromptu songs about himself in The Wind in the Willows. What does impromptu tell you about his songs? | He only sings them at Christmas | He has practised them for years | *He makes them up as he goes, without planning
test: Which sentence uses impromptu correctly? | We practised our impromptu song every night for a month. | *We had an impromptu picnic when the sun came out and we all decided to go. | Our impromptu trip was planned a year before we left.
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to impromptu? | *spontaneous | slow | careful | planned
